Here's my spending data. Write a weekly coaching note.

Week total: {{ $json.currency }} {{ $json.weekTotal }} across {{ $json.transactionCountWeek }} transactions
Month-to-date: {{ $json.currency }} {{ $json.monthTotal }}{{ $json.monthVsLastMonth !== null ? ' (' + ($json.monthVsLastMonth > 0 ? '+' : '') + $json.monthVsLastMonth + '% vs last month)' : '' }}
Total monthly budget: {{ $json.currency }} {{ $json.totalBudget || 'not set' }}
Essential spending: {{ $json.essentialPct }}% of monthly spend

Spending by category this week:
{{ $json.weekByCategory.map(c => `${c.category}: ${$json.currency}${c.total}`).join('\n') }}

Budget status this month:
{{ $json.budgetStatus.map(b => `${b.category}: spent ${$json.currency}${b.total}${b.budget ? ' / budget ' + $json.currency + b.budget + ' (' + b.pct + '%)' : ' (no budget set)'}`).join('\n') }}

Top merchants this month:
{{ $json.topMerchants.map(m => `${m.merchant}: ${$json.currency}${m.total}`).join('\n') }}

Biggest transactions this week:
{{ $json.biggestThisWeek.map(e => `${e.description}${e.merchant ? ' at ' + e.merchant : ''}: ${$json.currency}${e.amount}`).join('\n') }}

Over-budget categories: {{ $json.overBudgetCategories.length ? $json.overBudgetCategories.map(b => b.category).join(', ') : 'none' }}

Write the coaching note. Be specific about my actual numbers.

